---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="The First Strategy" description="A simple, three-principle system for testing a business idea using real money and real refusals, not opinions.">
  <section class="hero section--tight">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">The First Strategy</span>
      <h1>Most advice says build first, ask later. This framework starts with the sale.</h1>
      <p class="lede">The First Strategy is a simple, three-principle system for testing a business idea using real money and real refusals &mdash; not opinions.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">Why this exists</span>
      <h2>First-time entrepreneurs fail one of two ways</h2>
      <p class="lede">Jumping in without any real test of the risk, or over-researching until nothing ever launches. The First Strategy gives you a small, cheap way to find out what's actually true before you commit to either extreme.</p>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:640px;">Proof only counts if it's real: a completed sale, a clear refusal, or a deposit. Opinions, survey answers, and "sounds like a good idea" from a friend don't count &mdash; they don't involve real money or a real commitment.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">The three principles</span>
      <h2>Revenue First. Free First. Impact First.</h2>
      <div class="grid grid--3" style="margin-top:32px;">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Revenue First</h3>
          <p class="muted">The only signal that counts is a real transaction. If someone hands you money, or clearly refuses to, you've learned something real.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Free First</h3>
          <p class="muted">Run the free version of a test before you spend any money on it. A text message or a real conversation can test most ideas well enough to start.</p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Impact First</h3>
          <p class="muted">When you have more than one thing you could test, test the one most likely to move your business forward.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">What's in the full guide</span>
      <h2>Everything you need to run your first Proof Round</h2>
      <ul class="principle-list" style="max-width:640px; margin-top:24px;">
        <li>The Product Value Stack &mdash; Core Benefit, Point of Difference, X-Factor, Story, Proven Audience, Motivational Driver</li>
        <li>How to run a Proof Round, start to finish</li>
        <li>What to write down after every sales attempt</li>
        <li>How to sell when you don't own the customer relationship</li>
        <li>How to know when it's time to move to a real platform or store</li>
      </ul>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--alt">
    <div class="container">
      <div class="gate-card" style="max-width:640px; margin:0 auto; text-align:center;">
        <h2>Get the full Student Guide, free.</h2>
        <p class="muted">Enter your email and we'll send you the complete First Strategy framework &mdash; the Value Stack, Proof Rounds, and the exact questions to ask a buyer.</p>
        <!-- This form has no backend yet. Connect it to an email service (e.g. ConvertKit, Mailchimp, Formspree) before launch. -->
        <form class="field-row" style="justify-content:center;">
          <input type="email" name="email" placeholder="you@email.com" required />
          <button type="submit" class="btn btn--primary">Send me the guide</button>
        </form>
        <p class="fine-print">No spam. Unsubscribe anytime.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
